      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Since each dial has 10 numbers on it, we can choose any digit from 0 to 9 for the first dial. This gives us 10 possibilities.\n\nFor each of the remaining dials, we cannot choose the same digit as on the previous dial. So, we have 9 choices for the second dial.\n\nThen, for the third dial, we again cannot choose the same digit as on the second dial. Therefore, there are 8 choices for the third dial.\n\nThe total number of different settings possible is the product of these choices: $10 \\times 9 \\times 8 = \\boxed{720}$.The answer is: 720",
